      "text": "11 \u00d7 35 = 330 + 55 = 385.\n</answer>.<|User|>The answer is correct. Thank you for walking me through the steps.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! I'm glad you found the step-by-step explanation helpful. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any mathematical concept, feel free to ask. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using long multiplication?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! To solve the multiplication of 11 and 35 using long multiplication, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. Write the numbers one above the other, aligning them to the right.\n2. Multiply the top number (11) by the ones digit of the bottom number (5).\n3. Multiply the top number (11) by the tens digit of the bottom number (3), and remember to shift the result one place to the left.\n4. Add the two results together.\n\nLet's go through these steps in detail:\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nStep 1: Write the numbers one above the other, aligning them to the right.\n```\n   11\n\u00d7  35\n```\nStep 2: Multiply 11 by the ones digit of 35 (which is 5).\n```\n   11\n\u00d7  35\n-----\n   55  (This is 11 \u00d7 5)\n```\nStep 3: Multiply 11 by the tens digit of 35 (which is 3), and remember to shift the result one place to the left.\n```\n   11\n\u00d7  35\n-----\n   55\n+ 330  (This is 11 \u00d7 3, shifted one place to the left)\n```\nStep 4: Add the two results together.\n```\n   11\n\u00d7  35\n-----\n   55\n+ 330\n-----\n  385\n```\nTherefore, the product of 11 and 35 is 385.\n</answer>",
