      "text": "414.\n```.\n</answer>.<|User|>The answer is correct. Thank you for walking me through the steps.\n<|Assistant|>You're welcome! I'm glad you found the step-by-step explanation helpful. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any mathematical concept, feel free to ask. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the distributive property?\n<|Assistant|>\nCertainly! Using the distributive property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). For the problem \\(18 \\times 23\\), we can express 23 as \\(20 + 3\\). Therefore, we can rewrite the problem as:\n\\[18 \\times 23 = 18 \\times (20 + 3)\\]\nNow, we can apply the distributive property:\n\\[18 \\times (20 + 3) = 18 \\times 20 + 18 \\times 3\\]\nLet's solve each part separately:\n1. \\(18 \\times 20\\):\n\\[18 \\times 20 = 18 \\times (2 \\times 10) = (18 \\times 2) \\times 10 = 36 \\times 10 = 360\\]\n2. \\(18 \\times 3\\):\n\\[18 \\times 3 = 54\\]\nNow, we add the two results together:\n\\[360 + 54 = 414\\]\nSo, using the distributive property, we also get the same result: \\(18 \\times 23 = 414\\).\n</think>.<|Assistant|>",
