erefore, the product of 82 and 20 using the distributive property is 1640.\n</think>.\n<answer>Therefore, the product of 82 and 20 using the distributive property is 1640.</answer>.<|User|>This is very helpful. Could you also explain how to solve this problem using the area model method? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! The area model method is a visual way to multiply two numbers by breaking them down into smaller parts and then finding the area of rectangles. Here's how we can solve the problem of finding the product of 82 and 20 using the area model method:\n1. Break down 82 into 80 and 2.\n2. Draw a rectangle and divide it into two smaller rectangles. One rectangle will have dimensions 80 by 20, and the other will have dimensions 2 by 20.\n3. Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n   - The area of the first rectangle (80 by 20) is 80 * 20 = 1600.\n   - The area of the second rectangle (2 by 20) is 2 * 20 = 40.\n4. Add the areas of the two smaller rectangles together to get the total area, which is the product of 82 and 20.\nTherefore, the product of 82 and 20 using the area model method is 1640.\n</think>.\n<answer>Therefore, the product of 82 and 20 using the area model method is 1640.</answer>.<|User|>This is really helpful. Could you also show me how to solve this problem using the partial products method? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! The partial products method is a step-by-step approach to multiplying two numbers by breaking them down into their place values and then multiplying each part separately. Here's how we can solve the problem of finding the product of 82 and 20 using the partial products method:\n1. Break down 82 into 80 and 2.\n2. Write out the partial products for each part:\n   - 80 * 20\n   - 2 * 20\n3. Calculate each partial product:\n   - 80 * 20 = 1600\n   - 2 * 20 = 40\n4. Add the partial products together to get the final product:\n   - 1600 + 40 = 164