the area of a rectangle, where the length and width correspond to the factors. Let's use the area model to solve 43 \u00d7 88.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nTo solve 43 \u00d7 88 using the area model, we can break down each number into its tens and ones place values and then create a rectangle where one side represents the tens and the other side represents the ones. Here's how we can set it up:\n\n1. Break down 43 into 40 and 3.\n2. Break down 88 into 80 and 8.\n3. Create a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles, each representing the product of one part of 43 and one part of 88.\n\nThe area model would look like this:\n\n```\n  40 |  3\n-----|-----\n  80 |  8\n-----|-----\n  320|  24\n```\n\nNow, let's calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n\n- The area of the top-left rectangle (40 \u00d7 80) is 3200.\n- The area of the top-right rectangle (40 \u00d7 8) is 320.\n- The area of the bottom-left rectangle (3 \u00d7 80) is 240.\n- The area of the bottom-right rectangle (3 \u00d7 8) is 24.\n\nTo find the total area (which is the product of 43 and 88), we add the areas of the four smaller rectangles:\n\n```\n3200 + 320 + 240 + 24 = 3724\n```\n\nSo, using the area model, we also arrive at the same answer: 3724.\n</answer>",
