      "text": "91 \u00d7 76 = 6,776.\n```.\n</answer>.<|User|>The answer is correct. Thank you for walking me through the process.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! I'm glad you found the step-by-step explanation helpful. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any mathematical concept, feel free to ask. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the distributive property?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! The distributive property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. For the problem 91 \u00d7 76, we can express 76 as 70 + 6. Then, we can use the distributive property, which states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. Applying this to our problem:\n91 \u00d7 76 = 91 \u00d7 (70 + 6) = (91 \u00d7 70) + (91 \u00d7 6).\nNow, we can calculate each part separately:\n1. 91 \u00d7 70 = 6,370 (as we did before)\n2. 91 \u00d7 6 = 546 (as we did before)\nAdding these results together gives us the same final product:\n6,370 + 546 = 6,776.\nThis confirms our previous answer.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nUsing the distributive property, we can break down the multiplication as follows:\n91 \u00d7 76 = 91 \u00d7 (70 + 6) = (91 \u00d7 70) + (91 \u00d7 6).\nWe already calculated:\n91 \u00d7 70 = 6,370\n91 \u00d7 6 = 546\nAdding these results together:\n6,370 + 546 = 6,776.\nTherefore, the product of 91 and 76 is 6,776.\n</answer>.<|User|>That makes sense. Thank you for explaining both methods.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nYou're welcome! I'm glad you found both methods clear and helpful. If you have any more questions or need further explanations, feel free to ask. Understanding different methods can deepen your grasp of mathematical concepts. <|User|>Could you also show me how to solve this using the area model?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! The area model is a visual method that helps break down multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts. For the multiplication of 91 and 76, we can represent 91 as 90 + 1 and 76 as 70 + 6. The area model will then be a rectangle divided into four smaller rectangles, each representing the product of one part of 91 and one part of 76. Let's set up the area model and calculate the product.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nTo solve 91 \u00d7 76 using the area model, we can break down 91 into 90 + 1 and 76 into 70 + 6. The area model will look like this:\n\n```\n  90  1\n\u00d7  70  6\n------\n  6300  540\n+  70   6\n------\n  6776\n```\n\nHere's the step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **90 \u00d7 70**: This represents the area of the rectangle formed by 90 and 70.\n   ```\n   90\n\u00d7 70\n-----\n 6300\n   ```\n\n2. **90 \u00d7 6**: This represents the area of the rectangle formed by 90 and 6.\n   ```\n   90\n\u00d7  6\n-----\n  540\n   ```\n\n3. **1 \u00d7 70**: This represents the area of the rectangle formed by 1 and 70.\n   ```\n   1\n\u00d7 70\n-----\n  70\n   ```\n\n4. **1 \u00d7 6**: This represents the area of the rectangle formed by 1 and 6.\n   ```\n   1\n\u00d7  6\n-----\n   6\n   ```\n\nNow, we add all these areas together:\n```\n  6300\n+  540\n+   70\n+    6\n------\n  6776\n```\n\nSo, the product of 91 and 76 is 6,776.\n</answer>",
