pair of numbers and place the results in the appropriate cells:**.\n   - For 100 and $5.89:.\n     ```.\n     100 | 200 | 300 | 400.\n     5.89 | 589 | 1178 | 2356.\n     ```.\n   - For 200 and $7.99:.\n     ```.\n     100 | 200 | 300 | 400.\n     5.89 | 589 | 1178 | 2356.\n     1598 | 1598 | 3596 | 6992.\n     ```.\n   - For 300 and $4.99:.\n     ```.\n     100 | 200 | 300 | 400.\n     5.89 | 589 | 1178 | 2356.\n     1497 | 1497 | 2994 | 5994.\n     ```.\n   - For 400 and $6.99:.\n     ```.\n     100 | 200 | 300 | 400.\n     5.89 | 589 | 1178 | 2356.\n     2798 | 2798 | 5994 | 11992.\n     ```.\n\n3. **Add the numbers in the diagonals:**.\n   ```.\n   589.\n +1598.\n +1497.\n +2798.\n -----.\n 6482.\n   ```.\n\n   ```.\n   1178.\n +3596.\n +2994.\n +5994.\n -----.\n 13762.\n   ```.\n\n   ```.\n   2356.\n +6992.\n +5994.\n +11992.\n -----.\n 27334.\n   ```.\n\n   ```.\n   5992.\n +11992.\n -----.\n 17984.\n   ```.\n\n4. **Sum the totals:**.\n   ```.\n   6482.\n +13762.\n +27334.\n +17984.\n -----.\n 65562.\n   ```.\n\nSo, the total cost of purchasing all the items is $65,562.\n\n**Why the Lattice Method is Useful Here:**.\n- **Handling Large Numbers:** The lattice method is well-suited for handling large numbers like 100, 200, 300, and 400, making it easier to manage and reduce the risk of errors.\n- **Structured Approach:** The lattice method provides a structured way to break down the multiplication into smaller, manageable parts, which can be particularly helpful when dealing with multiple items and different prices.\n- **Visual Clarity:** The visual representation of the lattice can help students understand the process and verify their calculations.\n\nIn this example, the lattice method ensures accuracy and provides a clear, step-by-step approach to solving the problem, making it a valuable tool in real-world scenarios involving financial calculations. <|User|>This is really helpful. Can you give me another example where the lattice method might be particularly