messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 30 and 35? Please reason step by step.', '<think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 30 and 35, we can follow these steps:.\n1. Understand that the product of two numbers is the result of multiplying them together.\n2. Recognize that 30 and 35 are both multiples of 5, which might make the multiplication easier.\n3. Break down the numbers to make the multiplication simpler:.\n   - 30 can be written as 3 × 10.\n   - 35 can be written as 7 × 5.\n4. Now, we can rewrite the multiplication as:.\n   (3 × 10) × (7 × 5).\n5. According to the associative property of multiplication, we can rearrange the factors without changing the product:.\n   (3 × 7) × (10 × 5).\n6. Calculate the products inside the parentheses:.\n   3 × 7 = 21.\n   10 × 5 = 50.\n7. Finally, multiply the results of the two products:.\n   21 × 50.\n8. To make this multiplication easier, we can break it down further:.\n   - 21 × 50 = 21 × (5 × 10).\n   - 21 × (5 × 10) = (21 × 5) × 10.\n   - 21 × 5 = 105.\n   - (21 × 5) × 10 = 105 × 10.\n9. Now, multiplying 105 by 10 is straightforward:.\n   105 × 10 = 1050.\nTherefore, the product of 30 and 35 is 1050.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
