      "index": 0,
      "text": "264 + 2200 = 2464.\n```.\nSo, the product of 44 and 56 is 2464.\n</answer>.<|User|>That's correct! Can you also show me how to solve this using the distributive property of multiplication over addition? I find it helpful to understand different methods.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n<think>\nCertainly! Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition can simplify the multiplication process. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can apply this property to break down the multiplication of 44 and 56 into simpler parts. Specifically, we can express 56 as \\(50 + 6\\), and then distribute the multiplication over this sum. Let's go through the steps:\n..\n</think>\n<answer>\nUsing the distributive property, we can express the multiplication of 44 and 56 as:\n\\[ 44 \\times 56 = 44 \\times (50 + 6) \\]\nBy the distributive property, this becomes:\n\\[ 44 \\times 56 = 44 \\times 50 + 44 \\times 6 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each part separately:\n1. \\( 44 \\times 50 \\):\n\\[ 44 \\times 50 = 44 \\times (5 \\times 10) = (44 \\times 5) \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ 44 \\times 5 = 220 \\]\n\\[ 220 \\times 10 = 2200 \\]\n\n2. \\( 44 \\times 6 \\):\n\\[ 44 \\times 6 = 264 \\]\n\nNow, add the results of these two multiplications:\n\\[ 44 \\times 56 = 2200 + 264 = 2464 \\]\n\nSo, the product of 44 and 56 is 2464.\n</answer>",
