What is the quotient when 66 is divided by 27? Please reason step by step.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the quotient when 66 is divided by 27, we can use the standard long division algorithm. This involves dividing the digits of the dividend (66) by the divisor (27) step by step. Let's break it down step by step.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nFirst, let's set up the long division:.\n```.\n  27 ) 66\n```.\nWe start by looking at the first digit of the dividend, which is 6. Since 27 is larger than 6, we consider the first two digits of the dividend, which are 66.\nNow, we divide 66 by 27:.\n```.\n  27 ) 66\n  - 54\n  -----\n    12\n```.\n12 is the remainder when 66 is divided by 27. So, the quotient is 2 and the remainder is 12. Therefore, the quotient when 66 is divided by 27 is 2 with a remainder of 12.\n</answer>",
