y 300 by 7:\n     ```\n     300\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     2100\n     ```\n   - Multiply 40 by 20:\n     ```\n     40\n   \u00d7  20\n   ------\n     800\n     ```\n   - Multiply 40 by 7:\n     ```\n     40\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     280\n     ```\n   - Multiply 5 by 20:\n     ```\n     5\n   \u00d7  20\n   ------\n     100\n     ```\n   - Multiply 5 by 7:\n     ```\n     5\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     35\n     ```\n\n3. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - Add the results of the partial products:\n     ```\n     6000\n     2100\n     800\n     280\n     100\n     35\n   ------\n     9315\n     ```\n\nSo, the product of 345 and 27 using the partial products method is 9315.\n\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts, making it easier to understand and perform, especially for larger numbers.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nCertainly! Let's solve the multiplication problem 345 \u00d7 27 using the partial products method:\n\n1. **Break down the numbers into their place values:**\n   - 345 can be broken down into 300, 40, and 5.\n   - 27 can be broken down into 20 and 7.\n\n2. **Multiply each part of 345 by each part of 27:**\n   - Multiply 300 by 20:\n     ```\n     300\n   \u00d7  20\n   ------\n     6000\n     ```\n   - Multiply 300 by 7:\n     ```\n     300\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     2100\n     ```\n   - Multiply 40 by 20:\n     ```\n     40\n   \u00d7  20\n   ------\n     800\n     ```\n   - Multiply 40 by 7:\n     ```\n     40\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     280\n     ```\n   - Multiply 5 by 20:\n     ```\n     5\n   \u00d7  20\n   ------\n     100\n     ```\n   - Multiply 5 by 7:\n     ```\n     5\n   \u00d7   7\n   ------\n     35\n     ```\n\n3. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - Add the results of the partial products:\n     ```\n     6000\n     2100\n     800\n     280\n     100\n     35\n   ------\n     9315\n     ```\n\nSo, the product of 345 and 27 using the partial products metho