This method ensures that each digit of the multiplier is correctly aligned and multiplied, and the results are added together, providing a systematic and reliable way to perform the multiplication.\n</think>.\n<answer>. To solve \\( 25 \\times 820 \\) using the standard multiplication method, we follow these steps:\n\n1. Write the numbers one below the other:\n   ```\n   25\n   \u00d7 820\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 25 by 0 (the units digit of 820):\n   - \\( 25 \\times 0 = 0 \\)\n   - This results in 0, and we write it as:\n   ```\n   25\n   \u00d7 820\n   ----\n     0\n   ```\n\n3. Multiply 25 by 2 (the tens digit of 820), and shift one place to the left:\n   - \\( 25 \\times 2 = 50 \\)\n   - Shifting one place to the left gives us 500:\n   ```\n   25\n   \u00d7 820\n   ----\n     0\n   +500\n   ```\n\n4. Multiply 25 by 8 (the hundreds digit of 820), and shift two places to the left:\n   - \\( 25 \\times 8 = 200 \\)\n   - Shifting two places to the left gives us 20000:\n   ```\n   25\n   \u00d7 820\n   ----\n     0\n   +500\n   +20000\n   ```\n\n5. Add the results together:\n   - \\( 0 + 500 + 20000 = 20500 \\)\n   - Therefore, the final product is:\n   ```\n   25\n   \u00d7 820\n   ----\n   20500\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of \\( 25 \\times 820 \\) is \\( 20500 \\).</answer>",
