messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 30 and 42? Please reason step by step.', '<think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 30 and 42, we can follow these steps:.\n1. Understand that the product of two numbers is the result of multiplying them together.\n2. Recognize that multiplication can be done in any order, meaning 30 × 42 is the same as 42 × 30.\n3. To make the multiplication easier, we can break down the numbers into factors that are easier to work with. In this case, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition.\n4. We can express 30 as 3 × 10 and 42 as 6 × 7.\n5. Now, we can rewrite the multiplication as (3 × 10) × (6 × 7).\n6. Using the associative property of multiplication, we can rearrange the factors: 3 × 6 × 10 × 7.\n7. Calculate the products step by step:.\n   - 3 × 6 = 18.\n   - 10 × 7 = 70.\n   - Now, multiply the results: 18 × 70.\n8. To make 18 × 70 easier to calculate, we can break it down further:.\n   - 18 × 70 = 18 × (7 × 10).\n   - We can use the associative property again: (18 × 7) × 10.\n   - Calculate 18 × 7: 18 × 7 = 126.\n   - Now, multiply by 10: 126 × 10 = 1260.\nTherefore, the product of 30 and 42 is 1260.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
