      "text": "1260.</answer>.<|User|>The steps you provided are clear, but could you explain how the distributive property helped in simplifying the multiplication of 30 and 42? Also, could you show me how to verify the result using a different method? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly, I'll provide a detailed explanation of how the distributive property helped simplify the multiplication of 30 and 42, and then I'll show you a different method to verify the result.\n1. Distributive Property: The distributive property of multiplication over addition states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. In this case, we can express 30 as (3 \u00d7 10) and 42 as (6 \u00d7 7). We can use the distributive property to break down the multiplication as follows:\n   30 \u00d7 42 = (3 \u00d7 10) \u00d7 (6 \u00d7 7) = (3 \u00d7 6) \u00d7 (10 \u00d7 7) = 18 \u00d7 70\n2. Verification Method: We can verify the result by using the fact that multiplication is commutative, meaning that the order of the factors does not change the product. So, we can calculate 42 \u00d7 30 and see if we get the same result.\n   42 \u00d7 30 = (40 + 2) \u00d7 30 = 40 \u00d7 30 + 2 \u00d7 30 = 1200 + 60 = 1260\nSince both methods give us the same result, we can be confident that the product of 30 and 42 is indeed 1260.\n</think>.\n<answer>Using the distributive property, we can break down the multiplication of 30 and 42 as follows:\n30 \u00d7 42 = (3 \u00d7 10) \u00d7 (6 \u00d7 7) = (3 \u00d7 6) \u00d7 (10 \u00d7 7) = 18 \u00d7 70\nTo verify the result, we can use the commutative property of multiplication:\n42 \u00d7 30 = (40 + 2) \u00d7 30 = 40 \u00d7 30 + 2 \u00d7 30 = 1200 + 60 = 1260\nBoth methods give us the same result, confirming that the product of 30 and 42 is 1260.</answer>",
