onally**:\n   - Add the numbers in each diagonal, starting from the bottom right and moving to the top left. If the sum is a two-digit number, carry the tens digit to the next diagonal.\n\n```\n  8 | 9\n  -+---\n  6 | 7\n  8 | 9\n  -+---\n  48 | 63\n  54 | 63\n  54 | 63\n  102 | 126\n```\n\n5. **Combine the Results**:\n   - The final result is read from the top left to the bottom right.\n\n```\n  8 | 9\n  -+---\n  6 | 7\n  8 | 9\n  -+---\n  48 | 63\n  54 | 63\n  54 | 63\n  102 | 126\n```\n\nThe final product is \\(5963\\).\n\n### Summary\n- **Grid Setup**: Create a 2x2 grid.\n- **Multiplication**: Multiply each digit and place the results in the grid.\n- **Addition**: Add the numbers diagonally and carry over as needed.\n- **Result**: Read the final product from the top left to the bottom right.\n\nThis method provides a visual and systematic way to handle multiplication, especially useful for larger numbers. <|User|>This lattice method is really helpful! Could you also show me how to solve \\(76 \\times 51\\) using the lattice method? <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! Let's solve \\(76 \\times 51\\) using the lattice method.\n\n### Lattice Multiplication for \\(76 \\times 51\\)\n\n1. **Set Up the Grid**:\n   - Draw a 2x2 grid since \\(76\\) has 2 digits and \\(51\\) has 2 digits.\n\n```\n  7 | 6\n  -+---\n  5 | 1\n```\n\n2. **Write the Numbers**:\n   - Place the digits of the first number (76) along the top of the grid and the digits of the second number (51) along the right side of the grid.\n\n```\n  7 | 6\n  -+---\n  5 | 1\n```\n\n3. **Multiply Each Digit**:\n   - Multiply each digit of the top number by each digit of the right number and write the results in the corresponding cells of the grid. Place the tens digit in the upper triangle and the ones digit in the lower triangle.\n\n```\n  7 | 6\n  -+---\n  5 | 1\n  7 | 6\n  -+---\n  35 | 6\n  35 | 6\n```\n\n4. **Add Diagonally**:\n   - Add the numbers in each diagonal, starting from the bottom right and movin